# Preserve Manual Edits

Treat code the user edited by hand as intentional. Never revert, rewrite, or "clean up" those edits as a side effect of another request.

## Required behavior

- Before editing a region, check whether the user changed it manually (recent edit history, uncommitted diffs, or values that differ from what you previously wrote). If so, leave it alone.
- If a request cannot be completed without touching a manually edited region, stop and ask for explicit approval first, naming the file, the lines, and what would change.
- Only change a manual edit when the user explicitly asks for that specific change.
- When a manual edit conflicts with another rule or with your own earlier implementation, surface the conflict and let the user decide instead of silently resolving it.
- Scope edits tightly to what was requested; do not reformat, rename, or re-order surrounding manually written code.

## Examples

```jsx
// User manually changed gap={3} → gap={2} and the title copy.
<Flex gap={2}>
  <Title>Domain overview</Title>
</Flex>

// ❌ Avoid: restoring your original values while implementing an unrelated request
<Flex gap={3}>
  <Title>Domain Overview Header</Title>
</Flex>

// ✅ Preferred: add what was asked for, leave manual edits untouched
<Flex gap={2}>
  <Title>Domain overview</Title>
  <Badge>Connected</Badge>
</Flex>
```

If unsure whether an edit was manual, ask rather than overwrite.
